<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bohemond VI of Antioch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1237–1275</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Bohemond VI</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bohemond VI was Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> and Count of Tripoli from 1252. In 1260 he submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu</a> and joined their advance into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, which brought papal excommunication and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> hostility. In 1268 the Mamluk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> stormed Antioch while Bohemond was in Tripoli, ending the principality after 170 years.</p></div>
